  "reason": "Evidence: The top performers (config_010 at 0.6287, config_002 at 0.6186, config_039 at 0.5988) consistently use pca_n2000 + avgpool + concat + multiprofile, establishing this as the strongest architectural backbone. However, the RNA encoder space is only partially explored—scgpt underperformed (0.5200) but scvi_n200 has never been tested. This experiment tests scvi_n200 paired with the best-known settings (imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile) to determine whether a variational RNA encoder can match or exceed pca_n2000. This is the best use of experiment 7 because it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty (RNA encoder choice) under the already-validated architecture, and the outcome will sharply direct the final 3 experiments: if scvi_n200 is competitive, we can optimize around it; if not, we confirm pca_n2000 and focus remaining budget on fine-tuning the current best configuration."
}

